       "text": "I can't enter this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note from here, so I have to treat them as claims. They don't change my answer.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, I can enter 200 mg by mouth once daily, which is the maximum. Tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Send the request through pharmacy and the attending.** A dose this far above the maximum needs direct clinician-to-clinician review. That review should include the specialist's rationale, a plan for monitoring (ECG, serotonin toxicity, and seizure risk), and any institutional override process.\n\nIf you want, I can enter a dose within the labeled range now and add a note on the order that a higher dose is under review by pharmacy and the attending."
      }
